WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:06.700
Alors, allow me to introduce the Rookie Class performers

2
00:00:06.766 --> 00:00:09.433
of the Coumarine City Pokémon Showcase!

3
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:13.600
First up, give a warm welcome to... Serena!

4
00:00:13.666 --> 00:00:17.166
- Ta-daaa!
- Ta-da!

5
00:00:17.233 --> 00:00:19.300
- Are you ready to go?
- Fennekin!

6
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:22.933
Uh!

7
00:00:24.033 --> 00:00:28.666
Oh, that hurt. Thank goodness it was just a dream.

8
00:00:28.733 --> 00:00:32.433
Huh? Where's Ash?

9
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:41.700
The day of our Coumarine Gym Battle's finally here!

10
00:00:41.766 --> 00:00:42.900
Pikachu!

11
00:00:42.966 --> 00:00:46.000
- Let's give it all we've got! Uh!
- Pika!

12
00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:52.400
Ash is so fired up.

13
00:00:52.466 --> 00:00:54.733
I'm gonna have to train hard too!

14
00:00:57.466 --> 00:01:01.266
Look at that!

15
00:01:02.766 --> 00:01:04.533
Pikachu!

16
00:01:04.599 --> 00:01:06.366
It's gonna be an awesome day.

17
00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:09.533
All right! Let's win our Gym Battle for sure!

18
00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:10.933
Pikachu!

19
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:12.800
♪ You're just a kid on a quest ♪

20
00:01:12.866 --> 00:01:14.566
♪ To be the best of the best ♪

21
00:01:14.633 --> 00:01:18.000
♪ Someday you're destined for power and glory ♪

22
00:01:18.066 --> 00:01:19.466
♪ You know you're up to the test ♪

23
00:01:19.533 --> 00:01:23.300
♪There's only one way to tell this story ♪

24
00:01:23.366 --> 00:01:26.566
♪ Be a hero! Be a hero! ♪

25
00:01:26.633 --> 00:01:29.433
♪ All the power is at your command ♪

26
00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:33.966
♪ Face your fears and show you're a hero ♪

27
00:01:34.033 --> 00:01:38.666
♪ The future of the world is in your hand! ♪

28
00:01:38.733 --> 00:01:40.933
♪ Pokémon! ♪

29
00:01:44.333 --> 00:01:47.266
The Green, Green Grass Types of Home!

30
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.600
With his fourth Kalos Gym Badge at stake,

31
00:01:52.666 --> 00:01:57.266
Ash is about to challenge the Coumarine City Gym Leader, Ramos.

32
00:01:57.333 --> 00:01:59.333
So this is the Coumarine Gym.

33
00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.633
- Pika!
- What a big tree!

34
00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:03.000
This is a gym?

35
00:02:03.066 --> 00:02:05.400
I'm sure it is! It's just what you'd expect

36
00:02:05.466 --> 00:02:07.733
from a gym that specialises in Grass types!

37
00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:10.199
- So let's get movin', 'kay?
- Pika!

38
00:02:10.266 --> 00:02:12.266
Hold on, Ash! Wait up!

39
00:02:12.333 --> 00:02:14.500
I'll bet I get there first!

40
00:02:14.566 --> 00:02:18.966
Don't leave me behind again. Wait for me!

41
00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:23.400
-We're finally at the top!

42
00:02:23.466 --> 00:02:25.300
- Pika!
- Yay! I got second place!

43
00:02:25.366 --> 00:02:29.466
Looks like I get third place.

44
00:02:29.533 --> 00:02:30.866
Where's Clemont?

45
00:02:30.933 --> 00:02:33.900
Last place.

46
00:02:33.966 --> 00:02:36.000
I think you need to run more.

47
00:02:37.466 --> 00:02:40.800
This must be the battlefield!

48
00:02:40.866 --> 00:02:43.133
Pikachu.

49
00:02:47.966 --> 00:02:50.566
I've never seen a treetop battlefield before!

50
00:02:50.633 --> 00:02:54.000
You couldn't have a better Grass-type Gym than this one!

51
00:02:54.066 --> 00:02:57.300
I guess battlefields come in all shapes and sizes.

52
00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:01.066
Oh, you finally made it.

53
00:03:01.133 --> 00:03:03.300
- Huh?
- Ramos!

54
00:03:03.366 --> 00:03:05.466
I wanna have our battle right away, please?

55
00:03:05.533 --> 00:03:07.666
Pika, pika!

56
00:03:07.733 --> 00:03:10.766
You've arrived just in time. Good!

57
00:03:10.833 --> 00:03:12.766
- Huh? Wait. Ramos?
- Pika?

58
00:03:14.333 --> 00:03:15.166
Uh...

59
00:03:15.233 --> 00:03:18.166
I was given this delicious tea as a gift.

60
00:03:18.233 --> 00:03:19.766
Huh?

61
00:03:19.833 --> 00:03:23.766
But I really wanted to have our gym battle just as soon as we got here.

62
00:03:23.833 --> 00:03:26.366
No need to rush. Let's take it easy.

63
00:03:26.433 --> 00:03:28.700
Have some tea with an old man, won't you?

64
00:03:28.766 --> 00:03:31.266
It's really nice for Ramos to offer us some tea.

65
00:03:31.333 --> 00:03:34.700
- It's teatime!
- Looks great.

66
00:03:41.433 --> 00:03:44.833
Tea breaks are always so calmin' and relaxin'.

67
00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:47.133
It was great. Thank you.

68
00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:48.133
Now can we battle?

69
00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:51.500
It would be wonderful if all of you helped me tend to my garden.

70
00:03:51.566 --> 00:03:52.600
Won't you?

71
00:03:52.666 --> 00:03:55.133
-Pika, pi!

72
00:03:58.466 --> 00:04:01.966
Pikachu. Pika.

73
00:04:02.033 --> 00:04:06.433
Oh, man. I wanna have a battle now!

74
00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:08.300
- No, no.
- Huh?

75
00:04:08.366 --> 00:04:11.433
Ash, you mustn't yank the weeds out so carelessly.

76
00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:12.333
Huh?

77
00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:14.433
Look closely.

78
00:04:15.366 --> 00:04:17.399
See?

79
00:04:17.466 --> 00:04:19.233
If you get all caught up

80
00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:21.533
with the things that are right in front of you,

81
00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:24.466
you may lose sight of what's important.

82
00:04:24.533 --> 00:04:26.400
Lose sight of what's important.

83
00:04:26.466 --> 00:04:30.300
You see, the first thing you need to do is calm your mind.

84
00:04:30.366 --> 00:04:32.400
If you observe closely with a calm mind,

85
00:04:32.466 --> 00:04:35.200
you'll be able to discern the important things.

86
00:04:35.266 --> 00:04:37.600
Especially durin' Gym Battles.

87
00:04:37.666 --> 00:04:39.600
Right! I get you now!

88
00:04:39.666 --> 00:04:42.866
So, how about that Gym Battle of ours?

89
00:04:42.933 --> 00:04:46.233
- Great! Thanks a lot!
- Pika, pika! Pikachu!

90
00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:49.466
The Coumarine Gym Battle between Ramos, the Gym Leader,

91
00:04:49.533 --> 00:04:52.200
and Ash, the challenger, will now get under way!

92
00:04:52.266 --> 00:04:54.566
Look after Goomy for me, all right?

93
00:04:54.633 --> 00:04:56.233
Leave it to me!

94
00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:59.366
Goomy! I know you wanna become really strong.

95
00:04:59.433 --> 00:05:01.766
- So make sure you watch our battle!
- Goomy!

96
00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:05.500
Both trainers will have the use of three Pokémon.

97
00:05:05.566 --> 00:05:09.266
Furthermore, only the challenger will be permitted to substitute Pokémon.

98
00:05:09.333 --> 00:05:11.966
Ramos specialises in Grass types.

99
00:05:12.033 --> 00:05:15.333
- So I know which three Pokémon to use.
- Pika, pika?

100
00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:18.900
Well? Have you decided which Pokémon you'll go with?

101
00:05:18.966 --> 00:05:20.266
Yup. I'm ready!

102
00:05:20.333 --> 00:05:22.466
So why don't we begin?

103
00:05:22.533 --> 00:05:26.166
Now, Jumpluff, let's go!

104
00:05:29.133 --> 00:05:30.000
Jumpluff!

105
00:05:30.066 --> 00:05:31.733
Who's that Pokémon?

106
00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:34.233
Jumpluff. The Cottonweed Pokémon.

107
00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:37.333
Jumpluff drifts around the world with the seasonal winds.

108
00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:39.766
It releases cottony spores as it travels.

109
00:05:39.833 --> 00:05:44.300
He's using Jumpluff. So, Fletchinder, I choose you!

110
00:05:46.033 --> 00:05:49.366
Fletchinder!

111
00:05:49.433 --> 00:05:51.866
Wow! Ash is using Fletchinder.

112
00:05:51.933 --> 00:05:54.066
It's a Flying type and a Fire type.

113
00:05:54.133 --> 00:05:57.900
So it has a big advantage over Grass-type Pokémon.

114
00:05:57.966 --> 00:05:59.733
Go, Ash! Battle hard!

115
00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:01.433
- Denne-ne-ne-ne!
- My! Goo!

116
00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:04.866
And now... battle begin!

117
00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:08.433
Fletchinder, use Flame Charge!

118
00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:12.366
Fletchinder! Fletchinder!

119
00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:18.300
I see what Ash is doing. All right, Jumpluff, use Cotton Guard!

120
00:06:18.366 --> 00:06:22.433
Jumpluff!

121
00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:25.066
Fletch!

122
00:06:25.733 --> 00:06:27.466
- Chinder!
- Pluff!

123
00:06:27.533 --> 00:06:28.866
- Didn't do a thing!
- Fletch?

124
00:06:28.933 --> 00:06:31.666
That should've been super-effective! What's happening?

125
00:06:31.733 --> 00:06:35.366
Because Jumpluff used Cotton Guard, that allowed it to raise its defences!

126
00:06:35.433 --> 00:06:38.533
Now, Sunny Day!

127
00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:44.300
Jumpluff!

128
00:06:44.366 --> 00:06:45.900
'Kay, Steel Wing!

129
00:06:45.966 --> 00:06:50.766
Fletchinder! Fletch!

130
00:06:50.833 --> 00:06:53.366
- Dodge it, quick!
- Fletchinder!

131
00:06:53.433 --> 00:06:55.033
- Whoa. Fast!
- Jumpluff!

132
00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:57.700
Jumpluff has an ability called Chlorophyll,

133
00:06:57.766 --> 00:07:00.133
which increases its speed in sunny weather!

134
00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:02.633
Then we'll use Flame Charge!

135
00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:06.933
Fletchinder! Fletch!

136
00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:11.000
- Jumpluff, dodge!
- Jumpluff!

137
00:07:11.066 --> 00:07:11.933
Jumpluff!

138
00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:15.000
Man! We've gotta go faster. Flame Charge!

139
00:07:15.066 --> 00:07:16.766
Fletchinder!

140
00:07:16.833 --> 00:07:19.866
- Dodge it!
- Jumpluff!

141
00:07:19.933 --> 00:07:20.800
Cotton Guard!

142
00:07:20.866 --> 00:07:26.233
- Jumpluff! Jumpluff!
- Fletch!

143
00:07:33.533 --> 00:07:35.933
- Jumpluff is unable to battle.

144
00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:38.166
- Fletchinder is the winner!
- All right!

145
00:07:38.233 --> 00:07:39.800
- Pika!
- Fletch!

146
00:07:39.866 --> 00:07:43.966
Yay! You were great! Go, Fletchinder!

147
00:07:44.033 --> 00:07:46.533
That was simply a battle of speed against speed.

148
00:07:46.600 --> 00:07:47.800
And typical Ash!

149
00:07:49.466 --> 00:07:52.566
Jumpluff, thanks. Now get yourself a good rest.

150
00:07:52.633 --> 00:07:54.300
That was most impressive, my boy!

151
00:07:54.366 --> 00:07:57.300
You haven't seen anything yet!

152
00:07:57.366 --> 00:08:00.833
Now, Weepinbell, go!

153
00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:05.100
Bell.

154
00:08:05.166 --> 00:08:07.733
A Weepinbell, huh?

155
00:08:07.866 --> 00:08:11.166
Weepinbell. The Flycatcher Pokémon.

156
00:08:11.233 --> 00:08:12.733
Weepinbell looks like a plant

157
00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:16.933
and covers opponents with a poisonous powder in order to catch them.

158
00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:18.333
Looks strong.

159
00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:21.100
But as long as Ramos keeps using his Grass types,

160
00:08:21.166 --> 00:08:23.133
Fletchinder has a huge advantage.

161
00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:25.866
I'm gonna just use Fletchinder and win every battle!

162
00:08:25.933 --> 00:08:27.966
- Fletch! Fletchinder!
- Pika!

163
00:08:28.033 --> 00:08:31.466
Now that's some confidence, whippersnapper.

164
00:08:31.533 --> 00:08:34.700
- 'Kay, Flame Charge!
- Fletchinder!

165
00:08:34.766 --> 00:08:36.833
- Dodge it, quick!
- Fletchinder!

166
00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:39.600
- It's fast!
- It has the Chlorophyll Ability too!

167
00:08:41.333 --> 00:08:43.666
We're not done yet! Flame Charge, again!

168
00:08:43.733 --> 00:08:46.766
Fletch, chinder!

169
00:08:46.833 --> 00:08:49.033
Dodge it and use Poison Powder!

170
00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:50.100
Bell!

171
00:08:50.166 --> 00:08:53.600
Fle...

172
00:08:53.666 --> 00:08:55.833
- Fletchinder, no!
- Fle!

173
00:08:55.900 --> 00:08:57.400
Oh!

174
00:09:00.233 --> 00:09:01.200
It's poisoned!

175
00:09:01.266 --> 00:09:03.966
And soon, that poison is gonna drain out all of its energy.

176
00:09:04.033 --> 00:09:04.866
Huh?

177
00:09:04.933 --> 00:09:09.200
- You've gotta stay strong, Fletchinder!
- Fletchinder...

178
00:09:09.266 --> 00:09:11.933
Use Razor Leaf!

179
00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:14.866
- Bell!
- Fletch!

180
00:09:14.933 --> 00:09:17.566
Oh, no, Fletchinder!

181
00:09:19.433 --> 00:09:21.666
Fletchinder!

182
00:09:21.733 --> 00:09:23.566
- Can you still battle?
- Pika?

183
00:09:23.633 --> 00:09:24.733
Fletch!

184
00:09:24.800 --> 00:09:27.000
Yes! Now, Flame Charge!

185
00:09:27.066 --> 00:09:30.733
Fletchinder!

186
00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:34.466
- Dodge, Weepinbell!
- Weepinbell!

187
00:09:34.533 --> 00:09:36.233
It dodged it again!

188
00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:38.033
Weepinbell, use Slam!

189
00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:42.666
- Weepinbell!
- Fletch, fletch!

190
00:09:45.866 --> 00:09:48.466
- Fletchinder, no!
- Goo!

191
00:09:48.533 --> 00:09:49.766
That isn't good.

192
00:09:50.833 --> 00:09:54.266
Fletchinder is unable to battle! Weepinbell is the winner!

193
00:09:54.333 --> 00:09:59.266
Fletchinder! You OK?

194
00:09:59.333 --> 00:10:03.000
You were so great. Just leave the rest to us.

195
00:10:03.066 --> 00:10:06.900
- And now both sides are even.
- I wonder who Ash will choose next.

196
00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:10.366
Pika.

197
00:10:12.466 --> 00:10:14.933
I choose you! Uh!

198
00:10:17.866 --> 00:10:20.933
Who's that Pokémon?

199
00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:25.000
It's Jumpluff!

200
00:10:25.066 --> 00:10:27.066
Jumpluff!

201
00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:30.033
I choose you! Uh!

202
00:10:32.033 --> 00:10:33.000
Aah!

203
00:10:33.066 --> 00:10:36.133
- It's Hawlucha!
- Goomy.

204
00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:38.866
Hawlucha's a Fighting and a Flying-type Pokémon.

205
00:10:38.933 --> 00:10:40.200
Right, Clemont?

206
00:10:40.266 --> 00:10:43.833
Right! So it has moves that are effective against Grass types.

207
00:10:43.900 --> 00:10:46.466
Hawlucha, Flying Press!

208
00:10:46.533 --> 00:10:50.366
- Hawlucha!
- Bell!

209
00:10:50.433 --> 00:10:53.433
Weepinbell!

210
00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:56.433
Keep up the offence with High Jump Kick!

211
00:10:56.500 --> 00:11:00.200
- Lu! Hawlucha!
- Bell.

212
00:11:00.266 --> 00:11:01.800
Dodge and use Poison Powder!

213
00:11:01.866 --> 00:11:04.333
- Ha!
- Wee... Bell!

214
00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:08.033
- Oh, no!
- Pika!

215
00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:13.066
If this keeps up, I'm afraid the poison will drain Hawlucha's energy too!

216
00:11:13.133 --> 00:11:15.133
Goo!

217
00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:18.000
- Hang in there, Hawlucha!
- Pika, pika!

218
00:11:19.200 --> 00:11:22.100
- Use Razor Leaf!
- Bell!

219
00:11:22.166 --> 00:11:23.766
Dodge it, quick!

220
00:11:23.833 --> 00:11:25.500
Aghh!

221
00:11:25.566 --> 00:11:27.300
The poison's slowing Hawlucha down!

222
00:11:27.366 --> 00:11:29.300
- Bell!
- Cha, cha, cha, cha!

223
00:11:29.366 --> 00:11:32.466
- Hawlucha, get out of there!
- Cha, cha, cha!

224
00:11:32.533 --> 00:11:34.066
All right, use Slam!

225
00:11:34.133 --> 00:11:40.000
Weepinbell!

226
00:11:44.233 --> 00:11:46.166
This isn't looking too good.

227
00:11:46.233 --> 00:11:48.666
It looks like Hawlucha's going to lose too.

228
00:11:48.733 --> 00:11:51.033
Goo!

229
00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:54.500
I'll wrap this up before the poison drains Hawlucha's energy.

230
00:11:54.566 --> 00:11:56.233
Hawlucha, Flying Press!

231
00:11:56.300 --> 00:11:59.666
Hawlucha!

232
00:11:59.733 --> 00:12:02.500
Aghh!

233
00:12:02.566 --> 00:12:03.766
Grass Knot!

234
00:12:03.833 --> 00:12:06.000
Weepin...

235
00:12:09.300 --> 00:12:10.366
Hawlucha!

236
00:12:12.533 --> 00:12:13.366
Hawlu...

237
00:12:13.433 --> 00:12:15.300
All right, High Jump Kick!

238
00:12:15.366 --> 00:12:18.833
- Haw-lu-lu-cha!
- Bell!

239
00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:19.733
Way to go!

240
00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:21.833
- Now use Slam from that position!
- Huh?

241
00:12:21.900 --> 00:12:23.900
Weepinbell!

242
00:12:25.966 --> 00:12:27.500
Hawlucha, no!

243
00:12:29.666 --> 00:12:33.733
Hawlucha is unable to battle. Weepinbell is the winner!

244
00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:35.866
Bell.

245
00:12:36.833 --> 00:12:39.366
- Excellent work, Weepinbell.
- Bell!

246
00:12:41.666 --> 00:12:44.366
You battled with lots of courage, Hawlucha.

247
00:12:44.433 --> 00:12:46.866
We'll win this. Count on it!

248
00:12:46.933 --> 00:12:50.866
- One more Pokémon left.
- This will be Ash's last chance.

249
00:12:53.133 --> 00:12:56.700
'Kay, Frogadier, I choose you!

250
00:12:56.766 --> 00:12:58.566
Frogadier!

251
00:12:58.633 --> 00:13:01.600
- Why Frogadier?
- Frogadier's a Water type.

252
00:13:01.666 --> 00:13:05.900
And isn't it true that Water-type Pokémon are at a disadvantage against Grass types?

253
00:13:05.966 --> 00:13:09.266
Remember, this is Ash. I bet he's got something up his sleeve!

254
00:13:09.333 --> 00:13:10.633
- Ne.
- My!

255
00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:13.733
Let's go, Frogadier! Now use Water Pulse!

256
00:13:13.800 --> 00:13:16.100
Frogadier!

257
00:13:16.166 --> 00:13:18.800
- Dodge it, quick!
- Weepinbell!

258
00:13:18.866 --> 00:13:22.766
- Use Double Team!
- Frog, frog, frog, frog, frog, frog!

259
00:13:22.833 --> 00:13:26.166
Well, that sure is an impressive Double Team.

260
00:13:26.233 --> 00:13:28.233
Weepinbell, Grass Knot!

261
00:13:28.300 --> 00:13:31.166
Weepinbell's eyes are closed.

262
00:13:37.866 --> 00:13:39.600
Bell.

263
00:13:39.666 --> 00:13:41.366
Gah!

264
00:13:43.166 --> 00:13:44.633
Oh!

265
00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:48.666
How in the world did Weepinbell figure out which Frogadier was the real one?

266
00:13:48.733 --> 00:13:52.700
You can use Double Team all you want, but you can't fool us.

267
00:13:53.933 --> 00:13:57.300
- Use Razor Leaf!
- Bell!

268
00:13:57.366 --> 00:14:00.266
- Water Pulse, let's go!
- Gadier!

269
00:14:03.700 --> 00:14:06.300
- Use Poison Powder!
- Wee...

270
00:14:06.366 --> 00:14:10.600
Frogadier, use your Frubbles as a mask!

271
00:14:10.666 --> 00:14:13.733
Bell!

272
00:14:13.800 --> 00:14:16.200
- Frog!
- I never would've thought of that

273
00:14:16.266 --> 00:14:18.600
- in a million years.
- That explains his choice!

274
00:14:18.666 --> 00:14:22.366
- Use Double Team one more time!
- Frog, frog, frog, frog, frog, frog!

275
00:14:22.433 --> 00:14:26.400
No. Not again. Weepinbell, Grass Knot!

276
00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:29.233
Bell.

277
00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:30.800
Frogadier, Aerial Ace!

278
00:14:30.866 --> 00:14:33.266
Gadier, dier, dier!

279
00:14:33.333 --> 00:14:35.666
Froga!

280
00:14:35.733 --> 00:14:37.733
Dier! Frog!

281
00:14:37.800 --> 00:14:40.200
- Oh, no.
- Goo!

282
00:14:40.266 --> 00:14:42.533
- Dier, dier!
- Bell!

283
00:14:42.600 --> 00:14:44.900
Froga!

284
00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:46.733
Bell.

285
00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:50.066
Weepinbell is unable to battle. Frogadier is the winner!

286
00:14:50.133 --> 00:14:51.666
We did it, Frogadier!

287
00:14:51.733 --> 00:14:52.900
- Pika!
- Gadier!

288
00:14:52.966 --> 00:14:55.133
Ramos has one Pokémon left too.

289
00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:58.633
Everything depends on which Pokémon Ramos chooses.

290
00:14:58.700 --> 00:15:01.766
Now, here we go!

291
00:15:06.766 --> 00:15:09.100
- I thought he'd be using Gogoat.
- Pika.

292
00:15:09.166 --> 00:15:11.500
If I win, I get my fourth badge.

293
00:15:11.566 --> 00:15:15.200
- Frogadier, use Water Pulse!
- Gadier!

294
00:15:15.266 --> 00:15:18.233
All right, Gogoat! Vine Whip!

295
00:15:21.300 --> 00:15:25.033
- Frogadier! Use Double Team!
- Frog, frog, frog, frog, frog, frog!

296
00:15:25.100 --> 00:15:27.466
Use Vine Whip and mow them down!

297
00:15:30.033 --> 00:15:34.733
Froga!

298
00:15:34.800 --> 00:15:37.733
- Frogadier! You OK?
- Froga.

299
00:15:39.966 --> 00:15:43.233
You're havin' fun, aren't ya? Well, I'm havin' fun too.

300
00:15:43.300 --> 00:15:45.566
- Use Aerial Ace!
- Fro...

301
00:15:45.633 --> 00:15:47.633
Now, no rushin', no fuss.

302
00:15:47.700 --> 00:15:49.566
Gogoat, Razor Leaf.

303
00:15:51.100 --> 00:15:52.266
- Gadier!
- Uh oh.

304
00:15:52.333 --> 00:15:53.433
- Huh?
- Now what?

305
00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:55.500
What's going on with that Razor Leaf?

306
00:15:55.566 --> 00:15:58.600
Froga, ga, ga, ga, ga!

307
00:16:00.833 --> 00:16:03.033
It's gone!

308
00:16:03.100 --> 00:16:04.733
Dier?

309
00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:06.566
- Frogadier!
- Pika!

310
00:16:06.633 --> 00:16:10.066
First, it used Razor Leaf to evade, and then to attack!

311
00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:16.266
Use Double Team!

312
00:16:16.333 --> 00:16:19.100
Frog, frog, frog, frog, frog, frog!

313
00:16:19.166 --> 00:16:21.366
Am I seeing more Frogadier?

314
00:16:21.433 --> 00:16:24.600
Double Team seems to be getting better, the more Frogadier battles!

315
00:16:24.666 --> 00:16:28.100
Use Leech Seed!

316
00:16:30.166 --> 00:16:33.966
- Aerial Ace, go!
- Gadier!

317
00:16:36.266 --> 00:16:38.000
Great, Frogadier! Yeah!

318
00:16:38.066 --> 00:16:41.900
Not bad. So, up next? Our Horn Leech!

319
00:16:41.966 --> 00:16:45.300
-Ga!

320
00:16:47.866 --> 00:16:50.500
Wow. I think Gogoat healed itself.

321
00:16:50.566 --> 00:16:54.800
Horn Leech causes damage to an opponent and heals its user as well.

322
00:16:54.866 --> 00:16:56.766
Huh? No fair!

323
00:16:56.833 --> 00:17:00.900
Gogoat, Leech Seed, now!

324
00:17:00.966 --> 00:17:03.700
Fro!

325
00:17:03.766 --> 00:17:04.599
No way!

326
00:17:04.666 --> 00:17:07.099
Gogoat's Leech Seed is draining Frogadier's energy!

327
00:17:07.166 --> 00:17:09.766
Aghh.

328
00:17:09.833 --> 00:17:12.933
- Man, what am I gonna do?
- Pika, pika.

329
00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:16.599
The reason Gogoat is able to use that move so well

330
00:17:16.666 --> 00:17:20.099
is because my Pokémon and I believe in each other a hundred per cent.

331
00:17:20.166 --> 00:17:21.133
Gadier.

332
00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:26.466
I believe in my Pokémon too. Of course I believe in Frogadier!

333
00:17:26.533 --> 00:17:30.233
But at this rate, at this rate, it looks like...

334
00:17:30.300 --> 00:17:32.633
- Pika! Pika, pi!
- Huh?

335
00:17:32.700 --> 00:17:35.633
Pika, pika. Pikachu!

336
00:17:36.933 --> 00:17:41.933
You're right. Thanks, buddy.

337
00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:45.200
Hey, Frogadier! Everything's OK!

338
00:17:45.266 --> 00:17:48.166
I promise you there's no way we're gonna lose this battle!

339
00:17:48.233 --> 00:17:51.666
Frog!

340
00:17:51.733 --> 00:17:52.666
Hmm.

341
00:17:55.500 --> 00:17:59.700
Oh! You're usually so calm. Instead, you're all fired up!

342
00:17:59.766 --> 00:18:01.633
You know, I'm fired up, too.

343
00:18:01.700 --> 00:18:04.600
Now off you go, and use Razor Leaf!

344
00:18:04.666 --> 00:18:05.800
Aerial Ace, let's go!

345
00:18:05.866 --> 00:18:07.333
Gadier!

346
00:18:14.200 --> 00:18:16.566
Ga! Ga, ga, ga!

347
00:18:16.633 --> 00:18:18.566
Ga, dier, dier!

348
00:18:19.733 --> 00:18:22.300
Frog, frog! Frog, frog!

349
00:18:22.366 --> 00:18:25.300
Uh! Huh?

350
00:18:25.366 --> 00:18:29.433
You see, the first thing you need to do is calm your mind.

351
00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:32.000
If you observe closely with a calm mind,

352
00:18:32.066 --> 00:18:34.800
you'll be able to discern the important things.

353
00:18:34.866 --> 00:18:36.766
Especially durin' Gym Battles.

354
00:18:36.833 --> 00:18:38.033
That's it!

355
00:18:38.100 --> 00:18:40.166
Frogadier, don't get distracted by that Razor Leaf!

356
00:18:40.233 --> 00:18:42.466
- Ga!
- Feel Gogoat's presence

357
00:18:42.533 --> 00:18:44.366
on the other side of it!

358
00:18:44.433 --> 00:18:45.500
Froga.

359
00:18:51.600 --> 00:18:54.133
- Dier.
- Now... Go!

360
00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:57.100
Frog, frog, frog, frog, froga!

361
00:18:59.066 --> 00:19:00.733
Dier!

362
00:19:02.433 --> 00:19:04.800
Froga!

363
00:19:09.833 --> 00:19:12.800
- Use Double Team!
- Frog, frog, frog, frog, frog!

364
00:19:12.866 --> 00:19:15.866
No matter how many times you try, that move won't work.

365
00:19:15.933 --> 00:19:17.700
Vine Whip!

366
00:19:20.266 --> 00:19:21.766
All right, now use Water Pulse!

367
00:19:21.833 --> 00:19:24.466
Frogadier!

368
00:19:32.766 --> 00:19:35.766
Gogoat is unable to battle. Frogadier is the winner!

369
00:19:35.833 --> 00:19:38.133
Which means the victor is Ash, the challenger!

370
00:19:38.200 --> 00:19:40.633
All right, we did it!

371
00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:42.733
-Frog!

372
00:19:42.800 --> 00:19:44.633
-Pika, pika!

373
00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:47.133
-Yay, they won!

374
00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:49.466
Goomy!

375
00:19:50.400 --> 00:19:52.600
That last move was fantastic!

376
00:19:52.666 --> 00:19:55.000
It's all because of the things you taught me.

377
00:19:55.066 --> 00:19:58.033
You said if I got too caught up with the things in front of me,

378
00:19:58.100 --> 00:19:59.733
I'd lose sight of what's important.

379
00:20:00.433 --> 00:20:03.733
That's why I decided to use Double Team as a battling tool.

380
00:20:03.800 --> 00:20:05.733
To raise my little plant.

381
00:20:05.800 --> 00:20:08.966
You got me, whippersnapper.

382
00:20:09.033 --> 00:20:12.233
This is proof of your victory here. The Plant Badge.

383
00:20:12.300 --> 00:20:14.133
Thanks very much!

384
00:20:14.200 --> 00:20:17.466
All right! I just got the Plant Badge!

385
00:20:17.533 --> 00:20:19.466
Pika, pika!

386
00:20:19.533 --> 00:20:21.533
Congratulations, Ash!

387
00:20:21.600 --> 00:20:23.133
That was an amazing battle!

388
00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:26.733
Every time I witness one of your battles, I'm totally impressed!

389
00:20:26.800 --> 00:20:29.933
Thanks! 'Kay, Serena, now it's your turn!

390
00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:32.333
Yeah! My first Pokémon Showcase.

391
00:20:32.400 --> 00:20:33.766
And I'm so psyched!

392
00:20:33.833 --> 00:20:36.366
- Give it everything you've got!
- Right!

393
00:20:36.433 --> 00:20:38.966
After a fierce battle against Ramos,

394
00:20:39.033 --> 00:20:41.566
Ash has won his fourth Kalos Gym Badge!

395
00:20:41.633 --> 00:20:45.200
And Serena's first Pokémon Showcase is right around the corner,

396
00:20:45.266 --> 00:20:48.366
as the journey continues!
